# World scripts

markdoc-pdf shapes and renders many writing systems, not only Latin. Fonts are
chosen **per character**: the renderer walks a fallback list and uses the first
family that covers each codepoint, so one paragraph can mix scripts freely.
Right-to-left runs (Arabic, Hebrew) are shaped — joining letters into their
contextual forms — and reordered automatically.

The scripts below need their Noto fonts installed (`Noto Sans`,
`Noto Sans Arabic`, `Noto Sans Hebrew`, `Noto Sans CJK`, `Noto Sans Devanagari`,
`Noto Sans Thai`); any that are missing simply fall through to the next family.

## Greetings

| Language | Script | Greeting |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chinese (Simplified) | Han | 你好，世界 |
| Japanese | Kana + Kanji | こんにちは、世界 |
| Korean | Hangul | 안녕하세요, 세계 |
| Arabic | Arabic (RTL) | مرحبا بالعالم |
| Hebrew | Hebrew (RTL) | שלום עולם |
| Hindi | Devanagari | नमस्ते दुनिया |
| Thai | Thai | สวัสดีชาวโลก |
| Greek | Greek | Γειά σου Κόσμε |
| Russian | Cyrillic | Привет, мир |

## East Asian (CJK)

Chinese, Japanese and Korean share the Han ideographs but add scripts of their
own — kana for Japanese, hangul for Korean. All three are typeset from the same
pan-CJK font.

**Chinese** — 快速的棕色狐狸跳过了那只懒狗。文档可以用任何语言排版。

**Japanese** — 素早い茶色の狐が怠け者の犬を飛び越える。ひらがな、カタカナ、漢字。

**Korean** — 빠른 갈색 여우가 게으른 개를 뛰어넘습니다. 한글로 문서를 조판합니다.

## Right-to-left

Arabic and Hebrew read from right to left. The renderer shapes each run into its
joined forms and lays the runs out in visual order.

**Arabic** — الثعلب البني السريع يقفز فوق الكلب الكسول.

**Hebrew** — השועל החום המהיר קופץ מעל הכלב העצלן.

Bidirectional text mixes both directions: an Arabic phrase — مرحبا بالعالم —
inside an English sentence keeps each run in its own direction while the
sentence as a whole flows left to right.

## South & South-East Asian

**Hindi (Devanagari)** — तेज़ भूरी लोमड़ी आलसी कुत्ते के ऊपर से कूद जाती है।

**Thai** — สุนัขจิ้งจอกสีน้ำตาลที่ว่องไวกระโดดข้ามสุนัขขี้เกียจ

## European

**Greek** — Ταχεία αλεπού πηδά πάνω από το τεμπέλικο σκυλί.

**Cyrillic (Russian)** — Быстрая бурая лиса прыгает через ленивую собаку.
